---

The Core Problem: File-Based → Multi-User

Your current system uses local JSON files for state:

```
modules/[module]/party_tracker.json
modules/[module]/module_plot.json
modules/[module]/characters/*.json
modules/conversation_history/*.json
modules/campaign_summaries/*.json
```

For mobile multiplayer, multiple users cannot safely write to the same JSON files simultaneously. You need:

1. State Layer Migration

Current	Multiplayer Replacement	
JSON files on disk	Redis or PostgreSQL for real-time state	
`CampaignManager` (file-based)	`CampaignService` (DB-backed with locking)	
`StorageManager` (local files)	`StorageService` (DB transactions)	
`CompanionMemoryManager`	`NPCStateService` (shared across party)	

Why Redis specifically: SocketIO already pairs perfectly with Redis for multi-server scaling via `socketio.Server(client_manager=socketio.RedisManager(...))`.

